# Give a Matic bot's debug ethernet interface a recognizable name so the
# NetworkManager profile and the matic-debug-ip helper can find it on any USB
# port. Must sort before 80-net-setup-link.rules, or systemd's predictable
# naming (enpXsYuZ...) takes precedence.
#
# 0525:a4a1 is the generic Linux USB ethernet gadget ID, so the manufacturer
# string (the bot's Tegra USB controller) is required too; a Raspberry Pi or
# other gadget board must not end up named matic_*. The kernel version in that
# string changes with bot updates, hence the glob.
#
# Per-ifindex names, like the company's 61-matic-parallel-flash.rules, so
# several bots can be attached at once. Interface names are capped at 15
# characters; "matic_dbg" leaves six digits for the ifindex.
#
# The interface belongs to the bot (its Jetson exposes the gadget through the
# dongle's hub), so it only exists while the bot is powered.
SUBSYSTEM=="net", ACTION=="add", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0525", ATTRS{idProduct}=="a4a1", ATTRS{manufacturer}=="Linux * with tegra-xudc", NAME="matic_dbg$attr{ifindex}"
